  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "caption": "The key insight is that when the last characters match, they extend the common subsequence; otherwise I drop one of them and take the better result.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "var",
          "id": "a",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "name": "text1",
          "value": "\"abcde\""
        },
        {
          "type": "var",
          "id": "b",
          "x": 0,
          "y": 50,
          "name": "text2",
          "value": "\"ace\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "caption": "So I use a 2D DP where dp[i][j] is the LCS of the first i characters of one string and the first j of the other.",
